# Framing policy for the public projection.
#
# `_headers` is the static-host convention used by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. Vite
# copies this file verbatim into `dist/`, so the built output carries the policy with
# it instead of relying on whatever a host happens to default to.
#
# The embed views exist to be framed by someone else's site. Browsers allow that by
# default today, but a default is not a guarantee — a host that starts sending
# `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` or a restrictive CSP would break every embed silently.
# Declaring `frame-ancestors *` pins the intent. Replace `*` with an explicit
# origin list to restrict embedding to known partners; the syntax is the same.
#
# X-Frame-Options is deliberately absent: it has no "allow any origin" value, and
# modern browsers honour `frame-ancestors` over it anyway.

/embed/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *
